milar process to  why black things get hot in the sun  black dye is really good at absorbing  visible light and so it absorbs that  light the electrons in it get excited  and then it releases that energy back  out as heat  fireworks also work this way so the  electrons and fireworks  absorb the heat energy from the  explosives and then it releases that  energy back out as light  that's actually why we have different  colors there are different chemicals  inside the fireworks which release  different colors of light  now you might be wondering what sorts of  energy do sunscreen molecules release  then  it depends on which sunscreen chemical  you're talking about but it is usually a  combination of different types of energy  it can be vibrations which turn into  heat as those vibrations knock into  other molecules and those vibrations get  passed on  heat is really just vibrations it can be  lower energy forms of light so remember  you can't create energy out of nothing  so that sunscreen molecule might convert  part of the uv into a lower energy form  of light and the rest of it into heat  sunscreens can release infrared  radiation which turns into heat in your  skin  visible light or even lower energy forms  of uv  the uv can also turn into chemical  energy and what that means  is breaking bonds sometimes this is  reversible so the sunscreen molecule can  keep working  so the bond breaks and unbreaks as it  converts the uv energy into chemical  energy  just like we talked about before but  sometimes it's not reversible so that  means you don't get your original  molecule back  so your sunscreen slowly decomposes and  stops working over time  this is what happens when a sunscreen is  photo unstable  when formulators try to make a sunscreen  ingredient more photostable  basically what they're doing is trying  to convince that molecule to convert the  uv  energy into other forms of energy rather  than breaking the irreversible bonds  so with all this talk of heat you m